# What the engine cannot run without. `bash deploy/secrets.sh check` fails if any of these is
# missing from the encrypted store, so a move to a new provider finds out BEFORE the machine
# boots rather than after, when the failure reads as "All operators unavailable - check API keys".
#
# This list was taken from what is actually set on prospector-engine on 2026-08-18
# (`fly secrets list -a prospector-engine`), not from what someone thought was needed.
#
# Not every line here is a credential. R2_BUCKET and STORE_API_URL are addresses, and they are in
# the store rather than in stack.env because they are set the same way on every target - as app
# secrets - and splitting them across two files would mean two things to remember on a move.
#
# Deliberately NOT required: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (this estate has none and the engine rules on
# claude_cli, not the paid API), GEMINI_API_KEY and STANDARDCOMPUTE_API_KEY (both providers were
# deleted), DEEPSEEK_API_KEY and OPENROUTER_API_KEY (non-critical tiers that may be absent).

CONTROL_CENTER_PASSWORD
EXA_API_KEY
MINIMAX_API_KEY
PROSPECTOR_ENTITLEMENTS_API_KEY
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID
R2_ACCOUNT_ID
R2_BUCKET
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
STORE_API_URL
STORE_INTERNAL_API_KEY
STRIPE_LIVE_API_KEY
